    "content": "1\t# Task 13: Coral reef underwater with camera orbit\n2\t\n3\tBuild a single-page browser app with the provided framework, served by vite. It must render one full-viewport canvas with id #app. The scene is a shallow tropical coral reef seen underwater. Show a sandy seabed with rippled patterns, several coral formations in different shapes (branching, rounded brain, fan or tube shapes) and colours, and swaying seaweed or anemones. A school of at least 30 small fish should swim in a loose group, plus 2 or more larger solitary fish on their own paths. Sunlight should enter from above, with a bluish-green water tint, depth-based colour fade, and drifting caustic-like light patterns on the sand. A few bubbles or particles should rise slowly. The camera orbits slowly around the reef centre at a gentle height, with a slight bob, and no user input is needed. Do not rely on external downloads; build everything from simple procedural shapes.\n4\t\n5\tThe rendering contract in the next section applies.\n6\t\n7\t## Rendering contract (all tasks)\n8\t\n9\t- Draw into the existing `<canvas id=\"app\">` (640x360 CSS pixels, device pixel ratio 1). Do not resize it or create another canvas.\n10\t- Render continuously with `requestAnimationFrame`. When the first frame has been drawn set `window.__EVAL_READY__ = true`.\n11\t- No network access: load assets only from `/assets/...` (served from `public/assets`). Do not import from CDNs.\n12\t- Code goes in `src/` (TypeScript, strict). The entry is `src/main.ts`. It must"
